Title phone: after reset, set powerOn=true, bootT=2, screenBroken=false, protector=false, parts fine. G.phone.bootT maybe animate; mode title so update still runs? update loop will increment boot only when playing? I'll update boot whenever powerOn.

Task functions:
```js
function currentTask(){ return G.tasks[G.ti] || null; }
function installParts(){
 const seen=[]; G.tasks.forEach(t=>{ if(t.type==='install' && !seen.includes(t.part)) seen.push(t.part); }); return seen;
}
function partInstalled(part){
 if(!G.phone) return false;
 if(part==='screen') return G.phone.screenNew && !G.phone.screenRemoved;
 if(part==='protector') return G.phone.protectorNew;
 return G.phone.parts[part]==='new';
}
function traySlots(){
 const parts=installParts().filter(p=>!partInstalled(p));
 if(parts.length===0) return [];
 if(parts.length===1) return [{part:parts[0],cx:808,cy:400,w:104,h:214}];
 return [{part:parts[0],cx:808,cy:334,w:104,h:132},{part:parts[1],cx:808,cy:504,w:104,h:104}];
}
```
Careful: filtering installed parts changes slot positions after install; task completes anyway, so fine. But during dual job after battery installed and before screen install, tray would show only screen; okay.

For screen + battery initial two slots: screen first (part order from tasks: battery install then screen install → parts ['battery','screen']; first slot battery, second screen. Screen in 104×104 too small. Hmm. Need screen bigger. Sort parts by type so screen gets bigger? For two, allocate first slot 132 to screen if present. Use:
```js
parts.sort((a,b)=> (a==='screen'||a==='protector')?-1:1) // screen first
```
Then screen in slot1 104×132 (scaled .29 → 64×132) is small but acceptable. Better tray height 372; slots could be screen 190 and battery 100. Slot1 cy=335 h=160, slot2 cy=520 h=86. Screen 104×160 (scale .355 → 77×160), labels maybe cramped. Fine.

Let's set two slots: first (screen/protector) cy=338 h=170, second cy=520 h=90. For non-screen dual (none other with 2 parts). Good.

Sort so screen/protector first.

`traySlots` returns items even if installed? If installed, maybe show FITTED. I'd rather keep slots stable and show FITTED ✓ as in draw. So don't filter. Keep all install parts positions fixed. partInstalled draws FITTED. Dragging should only be allowed for current install & not installed. Fine.

So traySlots uses all installParts sorted.

Task start/set:
```js
function setTask(){
 const t=currentTask();
 if(!t){ renderTicket(); return; }
 t.progress = t.progress || 0;
 selectTool(t.tool);
 G.hold=null; G.drag=null;
 renderTicket();
}
```
But renderTicket is called on every step; also update hot tool class.

`selectTool(name)` updates G.selected and classes. Add hot class based on current task.

Tool buttons event listeners.

renderTicket builds list and now box. Use `textContent` to avoid injection; but need innerHTML with dots. Static data safe; use DOM creation.

```js
